## 3. Architecture Layers

```text
backend/src/{{ project_slug }}/
├── core/           # Domain — entities, interfaces, enums (NO external deps)
├── application/    # Use cases — services, DTOs, handlers (depends on core)
├── infrastructure/ # Adapters — DB, clients (implements core interfaces)
├── presentation/   # Delivery — FastAPI routes, GraphQL (depends on application)
└── composition/    # DI wiring (depends on all layers)
```

**Dependency rule (NEVER violate):**

```text
utils → config → core → infrastructure/ai → application → composition → presentation
```

---

## 4. Critical Rules

1. **Clean Architecture** — Inner layers never import from outer layers
2. **Type Safety** — All public functions must have complete type annotations; no `Any`
3. **Keyword-Only Args** — Functions with 3+ parameters use `*,` separator
4. **Structured Logging** — Use `structlog`, never `print()`; never log PII
5. **Factory Tests** — Use factory-boy for test data, never raw fixtures
6. **Conventional Commits** — `type(scope): description` format
7. **Registry First** — Never hardcode field/column names; use `registry/naming_registry.json`
8. **No Raw SQL** — SQLAlchemy ORM only
9. **Frozen Dataclasses** — `@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)` for value objects
10. **No secrets** — Never commit secrets; keep `.env.example` updated

